+      "content": "You know *por un lado* as an ordering marker from B1 Unit 23. This lesson uses it as the first half of a pair, to weigh two sides of one question:\n\n• *Por un lado, …; por otro (lado), …*: \"on the one hand … on the other\". Give one side first and the other second. Use it when something has an advantage and a drawback, or when there are two points of view.\n• *Por una parte, …; por otra (parte), …*: the same pair, a little more formal.\n• You can make the second half sharper with *en cambio*: *Por un lado, el piso es barato; en cambio, está lejos del centro.*\n\nPut a comma after each half-opener and a semicolon or a full stop between the halves. The second half needs *otro* or *otra*, never a second *un lado*."
     },
     {
